{
 "_meta": {
  "buffer_m": 750.0,
  "coordinate_fallback_m": 1000.0,
  "coordinate_rule": "coordinate_qc_fail when the resort point lies more than 1000 m outside its own boundary polygon. Those resorts also fall back off the unified path, NOT because their elevations are wrong (all 11 pass elevation QC) but because resort lat/lon is the query coordinate for every upstream request and cell_selection=nearest pins the model grid cell to it. Coordinates are NOT auto-corrected here; that is a separate track with its own full-forecast regression.",
  "elevation_rule": "quarantine iff declared > polygon_dem_max + tolerance AND declared > buffered_polygon_dem_max + tolerance. Two sources that fail in OPPOSITE directions: an OSM polygon can under-map an upper sector (reads too low), and a point-centred box samples a different mountain when the coordinate is wrong. The earlier point-centred +/-3 km box is NOT an input here \u2014 measured against the polygon pair it produced 11 flags of which 1 survived, a 91% false-positive rate.",
  "generated_utc": "2026-08-18",
  "no_polygon": "qc_unverified_no_polygon: never quarantined. The box alone cannot separate a real error from its own leakage, so absence of evidence is recorded as such.",
  "quarantine_tolerance_m": 500.0,
  "regenerate": "Re-run when the boundary cache, the curated elevations, or the resort coordinates change. Nothing detects those automatically.",
  "resorts": 58,
  "thresholds_are_provisional": "quarantine_tolerance_m and buffer_m are fleet-QC tuning values set from one fleet snapshot. They are not physical constants and must not be treated as such.",
  "what": "Per-resort, per-band input QC for the unified band-thermodynamic snow path. Two INDEPENDENT axes: elevation_qc asks whether a declared band exists on this mountain, coordinate_qc asks whether this is the right mountain. They are not merged, because a wrong coordinate misdirects every upstream request while a wrong band elevation biases one number."
 },
